label("$D$", D, NW);
label("$\theta$", (0.5,0.3));
label("$62^\circ$", (0.5,0.6));
label("$75^\circ$", (0.3,0.7));
[/asy]

Since $\overline{AB} \parallel \overline{CD}$ and $\overline{AD} \parallel \overline{BC}$, opposite angles are equal, and adjacent angles are supplementary. Hence, $\angle A = \angle C = 62^\circ$ and $\angle B = \angle D = 180^\circ - 62^\circ = 118^\circ$.

Since $\angle ADB = 75^\circ$, $\angle ABD = 180^\circ - \angle A - \angle ADB = 180^\circ - 62^\circ - 75^\circ = 43^\circ$.

Therefore, $\angle BDC = \angle ABD = \boxed{43^\circ}$.
The answer is $\boxed{43}$.

