\[\sum_{1 \le i < j \le 144} a_i a_j = 10140 - 2S,\]where $S$ is the number of pairs $(i,j)$ such that $a_i a_j = -1.$

Suppose that at least one of the $a_i$ is equal to $1.$  Then we can choose $a_j = -1,$ where $j \neq i,$ and $a_k = 1$ for all other $k,$ to make $S$ as large as possible.  This makes $S$ equal to $10139,$ so
