label("$B$", (0,60), W);
label("$30$", (60,30), E);

[/asy]

This region is a right triangle with base and height both equal to 30 units. Therefore, its area is $(1/2)(30)(30) = 450$ square units.

The area of the square is $(60)(60) = 3600$ square units. Therefore, the probability that Alice and Bob are less than 30 minutes late for the party is the ratio of the area of the triangle to the area of the square, which is $450/3600 = \boxed{\frac{3}{24}} = \boxed{\frac{1}{8}}$.

